<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Paris (1259)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1259">1259</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Paris of 1259 was agreed between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a>. Henry gave up his claims to Normandy, Anjou, Maine and Poitou, lost under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a>, and in return held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> as a duchy for which he paid homage to the French king. The arrangement over Aquitaine became a lasting source of conflict that helped cause the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1259.jpg" alt="Treaty of Paris (1259)" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trait%C3%A9_Paris_1259.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Treaty of Paris</b> of 1259, in which Henry III renounced his claim to Normandy, left the islands in English hands.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bailiwick-of-jersey">Bailiwick of Jersey · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>By the <b>Treaty of Paris</b> of 1259 Henry III of England gave up his claims to Normandy, Anjou and Poitou and did homage to Louis IX for a duchy reduced to Gascony, or Guyenne, with promises of lands in the Limousin, Périgord, Quercy and Agenais.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Duchy of Aquitaine · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Normandy was annexed to the French royal domain, and Henry III of England formally renounced his claim in the <b>Treaty of Paris</b> of 1259.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Duchy of Normandy · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Kings Louis IX of France and Henry III of England signed the <b>Treaty of Paris</b>, by which Henry gave up his claims to Normandy, Anjou, Maine and Poitou and held Gascony as a duchy, paying homage for it to the French king.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-4">4 December in history</a></li></ul></section>
